# Obra Product — PRD & Implementation Plan

## Executive summary

Obra’s product is an end-to-end contractor website factory inside one TanStack Start app (Lovable Cloud + Supabase). **v1 build path:** admin kickoff creates a **DB-only profile** (no auth user yet) keyed by `license_number`; admin runs the agent at `/user/<user-id>` on the contractor’s behalf and pitches the result. Contractor later **subscribes on the website** (checkout UI deferred; **post-checkout flow** is specified below). After payment: auth user created via OTP, linked to the existing license row by `license_number` + `email` pair; contractor then accesses `/user/<user-id>` to continue. Sites publish at `https://obra-tech.lovable.app/lp/<websiteId>`. LP enquiry flow stays unchanged.

**Current baseline:** single landing page at [`src/routes/index.tsx`](src/routes/index.tsx), lead-capture dialog, one Supabase table (`plan_inquiries`), no auth routes, no chat, no payments, no site renderer.

**Recommended delivery:** 4 phases (not one monolith). Each phase ships a complete user-visible slice. Assumptions called out where your prompt leaves forks open.

