```

### Journey B — Contractor post-checkout access (specified; checkout UI deferred)

```mermaid
flowchart TD
  Pitch[Admin pitched live preview] --> Checkout[Contractor subscribes on website]
  Checkout --> Capture[Checkout captures email license name city etc]
  Capture --> Pay[Payment completes]
  Pay --> Otp[OTP sent to email]
  Otp --> Link[Auth user created + linked to license row]
  Link --> UserChat[Contractor accesses /user/<user-id> agent chat]
```

- Checkout form fields become **account context**: email, license number, name, city, etc.
- If `license_number` matches admin-created row → link auth user to existing profile + website.
- If no match → new profile row created for auth user with submitted license + email.
- Each activated auth user has a unique **`(license_number, email)`** pair stored on the profile.
- **License collision at checkout:** if `license_number` already has `auth_user_id` set → reject (“License already activated — log in instead”). If `auth_user_id` is null (admin kickoff row) → link incoming checkout email to that profile.

### Journey C — Returning contractor (OTP)

- `/login` → license **or** email → OTP → `/user/<user-id>`.
- Session expiry → `/login` → OTP again. No passwords.

### Journey D — Admin operator

- `/admin` → view users, websites, conversations, edits, **leads** → kickoff → admin drives `/user/<user-id>` until pitch handoff.

