## Functional requirements

### 1. Subscription / checkout

**Checkout UI:** deferred — LP enquiry flow unchanged; no checkout routes in v1 implementation.

**Post-checkout flow (specified — build this):**

Split across two server functions with clear boundaries:

| Step | Function | When | Does |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | `completePostCheckout` | Payment webhook / stub fires | Persist checkout context (email, license, name, city) to `checkout_sessions`; create `subscriptions` row (`status=pending_activation`); **send Lovable OTP** to checkout email; redirect to OTP page. Does **not** create auth user. |
| 2 | `verifyOtpAndLinkProfile` | User submits OTP | Verify OTP → **create Supabase auth user** → link `auth_user_id` to profile by `license_number` (or create new profile if no match) → set `subscriptions.status=active` → redirect to `/user/<profiles.id>`. |

Numbered user-visible flow:
1. Contractor completes subscription on website (checkout UI wired later).
2. Checkout captures **email, license number, name, city**, and related context.
3. Payment completes → `completePostCheckout` runs (step 1 above).
4. OTP verified → `verifyOtpAndLinkProfile` runs (step 2 above).
5. Contractor lands on `/user/<profiles.id>` agent chat.

**v1 testing without checkout UI:** Admin dashboard **“Simulate subscription”** action (or dev-only `simulatePostCheckout` server fn) accepts license + email + name + city, skips payment, and runs `completePostCheckout` → OTP flow. This is how Phase 1 exit criteria (“contractor can OTP-login”) is tested before checkout routes exist.

### 2. Account creation & auth (OTP-only)

**Admin kickoff (pre-auth):**
- Creates `profiles` + `websites` stub only — **`auth_user_id` = null**.
- Admin session accesses `/user/<user-id>` via admin impersonation (service-role); contractor has no login yet.

**Post-checkout (contractor auth):**
- Auth user created only inside `verifyOtpAndLinkProfile` (after OTP verify), never in `completePostCheckout`.
- Link to existing `profiles` row by `license_number` if present (`auth_user_id` null); else create new profile.
- On link: set `profiles.email` from checkout context; enforce unique **`(license_number, email)`** composite.
- Lovable email-OTP + Supabase Auth session; no passwords.

**Identity policy (G3):**
- `license_number` UNIQUE → one business profile per license.
- One `auth_user_id` per profile (one contractor login per license).
- Checkout email becomes `profiles.email` at activation.
- Login with license/email must match the activated `(license_number, email)` pair.

**Admin impersonation (pre-auth kickoff):**
- `adminImpersonateUser(profileId)` sets httpOnly cookie `obra_impersonate_profile_id` alongside admin session.
- Server functions validate admin session + impersonation cookie; use service role for reads/writes scoped to that `profiles.id`.
- Impersonation does **not** create a contractor Supabase session; cookie cleared on admin logout.
- Contractor cannot access `/user/<id>` until post-checkout OTP completes.

**Edge cases:**
- License not found at login → “Subscribe to get started.”
- License found but `auth_user_id` null → “Complete subscription to activate account.”
- License already activated, checkout with different email → reject at `completePostCheckout`.
- OTP expired → retry with rate limit.
- Admin re-kickoff on existing license → resume website flow, don’t duplicate profile.

### 3. Agent onboarding chat (`/user/<user-id>`)

**UX target (GPT-5.5 via Lovable AI):** streaming tokens, **markdown rendering**, **rich text**, **scroll behavior** (auto-scroll to latest; preserve position on history load), **mobile chat layout**, **real-time tool-call status streaming** in chat (e.g. “Searching Yelp…”, “Generating variant 1…”, progress %), stop button, retry. **Inline structured widgets** for onboarding fields.

**Onboarding fields (agent must collect before generation):**

| Field | Input type | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| Registered business name | Text (widget or chat) | Pre-filled from admin kickoff when set |
| License number | Text | Pre-filled from admin kickoff; unique business key |
| **Trade / CSLB classification** | Select (e.g. C-33, C-36, B) | Required for Firecrawl + BUSINESS-CASE enrichment |
| Services offered | Multi-select + free text | Trade-specific defaults |
| Theme | Light / Dark | Inline widget |
| Primary color | Color picker (hex) | Optional — agent assigns default if skipped |
| Look & feel | Professional / Funky / Modern | Inline widget |
| Location | **California city picker** | v1 CA-only |

**Look & feel prompt profiles (agent system context):**

- **Professional:** restrained typography, navy/slate palette, credentials-forward hero, formal copy, minimal motion.
- **Funky:** bold colors, playful headings, asymmetric layouts, energetic microcopy.
- **Modern:** clean sans, generous whitespace, card-based sections, subtle gradients, contemporary contractor SaaS aesthetic.

**Memory model:**
- `conversations` + `messages` tables (full transcript).
- `onboarding_state` JSON on `websites` for structured fields extracted so far.
- **Journal artifact:** after every **10 messages (user + assistant combined, per `conversation_id`)**, append a new summary section to `journal-<license-number>.md` in **Supabase Storage** (`journals/` bucket) — first-class artifact loaded with system prompt + tool registry each turn. Counter is cumulative per conversation; license-number change case ignored (G9).
- Resume: on return, agent reads `onboarding_state` + latest journal + last summary → continues where left off.

**File picker (chat, media edit, gallery — same allowed formats):**
- **Images:** png, jpg, jpeg, webp, hevc
- **Video:** mp4, gif
- Upload to Supabase Storage; pass URLs to agent tools.

**Edge cases:**
- User skips required field → agent re-asks; block generation until complete.
- User changes answers mid-flow → update structured state; invalidate prior generated variants.
- User closes tab → state persisted; resume on next login.
- Agent timeout / API error → retry UI; message marked failed.

### 4. Enrichment (post-collection, pre-generation)

**Goal:** Populate contractor profile to the **full BUSINESS-CASE enrichment schema** (113 columns per `BUSINESS-CASE.md` §5) using **Firecrawl API**. **v1 geography: California only.**

**Firecrawl operator behavior:**
- Agent calls deterministic tool `firecrawl_scrape` (not free-form fetch).
- Runs as **sequential background jobs** (one platform/step per job) with **progress %** shown to user (e.g. “Enriching… 42%”).
- Tool builds **custom deep-search extraction instructions** from onboarding inputs: registered business name, license number, trade/classification, CA city, services offered.
- Instructions target all BUSINESS-CASE sections: CSLB deep pull, Google Business, Yelp, BuildZoom, Angi, Thumbtack, Facebook, Instagram, BBB, Houzz, HomeAdvisor, Nextdoor, aggregates.
- Firecrawl responses parsed into `contractor_profiles.enrichment_json` (113-column schema).
- `research_status` on `contractor_profiles`: `complete` | `partial` | `failed` | **`no_results_found`**
- **`websites.research_status`** mirrors `contractor_profiles.research_status` so UI/admin can show enrichment state on the website record without joining (G6). When deep search finds nothing, both rows show `no_results_found` and agent informs user honestly. Both update atomically when an enrichment job chain completes. `site_generation` job failures do **not** change `research_status`.

**G6 explained:** `contractor_profiles.research_status` is the enrichment source of truth. `websites.research_status` mirrors it so admin dashboard and `/user` UI can read enrichment state from the website row without a join.
- **Review/legal compliance (BUSINESS-CASE):** reviewer last names stripped to first-initial; source badges on review cards; only publicly visible data scraped.
- Agent may only cite enrichment fields present in `enrichment_json`.

**Pipeline:**

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
  participant Agent
  participant JobQueue as background_jobs
  participant FirecrawlTool as firecrawl_scrape
  participant Firecrawl as Firecrawl API
  participant DB as Supabase

  Agent->>JobQueue: enqueue sequential platform jobs
  loop Each platform
    JobQueue->>FirecrawlTool: deep search step
    FirecrawlTool->>Firecrawl: scrape + extract
    Firecrawl-->>FirecrawlTool: partial data
    FirecrawlTool->>DB: merge into enrichment_json
    JobQueue-->>Agent: progress % update
  end
  FirecrawlTool->>DB: final research_status
```

**Edge cases:**
- Ambiguous business name (collision) → agent asks user to confirm correct entity (Yelp URL / city).
- Scrape blocked (Facebook, rate limits) → store `research_status=partial`, continue with user-provided data.
- No web presence / deep search empty → `research_status=no_results_found`; generation uses onboarding inputs only with neutral copy.
- Invalid license → flag in admin; don’t block preview but show “unverified license” internally.

### Background job runner architecture (G7)

**Problem:** Firecrawl enrichment and site generation exceed HTTP timeouts. Jobs run sequentially, report progress %, and stream status to chat in real time (G13).

```mermaid
flowchart TD
  AgentTool["Agent calls firecrawl_scrape or generateVariants"] --> Enqueue["Insert job chain into background_jobs"]
  Enqueue --> Return["Return immediately to agent"]
  Runner["Job runner on Cloudflare"] --> Claim["Claim next eligible job in chain"]
  Claim --> Execute["Execute handler server-side"]
  Execute --> Update["Update progress_pct + status_message"]
  Update --> Realtime["Supabase Realtime broadcasts to chat UI"]
  Execute --> Complete{Last in chain?}
  Complete -->|yes| Mirror["Set research_status on contractor_profiles + websites"]
  Complete -->|no| Claim
```

**`background_jobs` extended columns:** `chain_id`, `sequence_index`, `platform`, `status_message`, `payload_json`, `error_message`, `idempotency_key`, `attempts`/`max_attempts`, `locked_at`/`locked_by`, `started_at`/`completed_at` (in addition to existing `id`, `website_id`, `job_type`, `status`, `progress_pct`, `result_json`).

**Enqueue pattern:**
- `firecrawl_scrape` does **not** call Firecrawl inline. Creates one `chain_id` + N `enrichment_platform` jobs (BUSINESS-CASE platform order: CSLB → Google → Yelp → …).
- `generateVariants` creates one `site_generation` job chain.
- Agent receives chain id immediately; tells user enrichment/generation started.

**Runner (Cloudflare Worker or scheduled server function):**
1. Claim next job where `status=pending` AND (`sequence_index=0` OR all jobs in same `chain_id` with lower `sequence_index` are `completed`).
2. Optimistic lock: `UPDATE … WHERE status=pending AND locked_at IS NULL`.
3. Execute: enrichment calls Firecrawl per platform; generation writes 2 `website_versions`.
4. Update `progress_pct` + `status_message` incrementally during execution.
5. On step complete: merge into `contractor_profiles.enrichment_json`; advance chain.
6. On enrichment chain complete: compute final `research_status`; write to **both** `contractor_profiles` and `websites`.
7. On failure after retries (`max_attempts=3`, exponential backoff): mark job `failed`; set `research_status=partial` or `failed`.

**Real-time progress (G13):**
- **Primary:** Supabase Realtime subscription on `background_jobs` filtered by `website_id` → chat UI tool-status bubbles.
- **Fallback:** `getJobProgress` polling on reconnect.
- **Agent SSE** (`sendAgentMessage`) streams LLM tokens only — does **not** duplicate job status (avoids double bubbles).

**Idempotency:** `idempotency_key = hash(website_id + job_type + chain_version)`. Re-trigger cancels pending jobs in prior chain (`status=cancelled`) and starts new `chain_id`.

### 5. Website generation (2 variants)

**User sees:** “We’re building your sites…” with progress % → two variant cards in inline preview panel → select one → approve or edit.

**Aesthetic & UX requirements (non-negotiable):**
- Generated sites must follow established UI/UX principles: clear visual hierarchy, readable typography scale, sufficient contrast (WCAG AA), consistent spacing, mobile-first responsive layout, accessible focus states, purposeful whitespace.
- Agent selects components from the **UI Component Library** (see § UI Component Library) — never ad-hoc unstyled markup.
- Primary color from onboarding (or agent-assigned default) applied consistently across CTAs, accents, and links.
- Light/dark theme choice drives background, text, and card surface tokens.

**Anti-hallucination, persona-first design & variant uniqueness:**
- **Persona-first (system prompt):** agent must recursively understand the contractor’s persona from first principles (trade, service area, enrichment data, look-and-feel) and design a site that **strictly caters to that persona** — not a generic template.
- Site copy grounded in `enrichment_json` or user inputs only — never invent ratings, reviews, license details, or service claims.
- If a field is missing, omit or use neutral placeholder copy — never fabricate.
- **Two variants must be visually distinct** — not two similar layouts. Enforced by deterministic `variant_key` using orthogonal dimensions (hero layout, section order, typography, palette from primary color).
- **Variant selection:** user previews both inline, explicitly **selects one**; unselected variant saved to history (`status=discarded`, not deleted).
- **Previous designs:** hamburger menu → “Previous designs” lists all past variants (selected + discarded) for this license/user; user can revisit but not auto-replace live site without re-approve.
- Edge cases: user previews A, selects B, edits B, then wants A → can switch from Previous designs → re-approve; regenerate one variant only; reject both → adjust look-and-feel and regenerate pair.

**Technical approach:**
- Agent/tool pipeline outputs `site_config` JSON (sections, copy, colors, theme, reviews, services, contact, media refs, `component_ids[]` from library).
- Template renderer: [`src/components/site-renderer/`](src/components/site-renderer/) reads config + resolves library components → React page.
- Generate **two variants** per job: different `variant_profile` (layout mood, palette, typography, hero layout) derived from look-and-feel + primary color + deterministic hash salt.
- Store as `website_versions` rows: `version_number`, `config_json`, `variant_key`, `status` (`draft` | `selected` | `discarded` | `live`).

**Edge cases:**
- Generation failure on one variant → show single variant + “regenerate second option”.
- User rejects both → agent conversation branch to adjust look-and-feel and regenerate.
- Large images → optimize on upload; max file size enforced.

### 6. Preview, approve, edit

**Preview (inline within `/user/<user-id>`):**
- Draft variants render in an **inline viewer panel** beside/below the agent chat — not a separate fullscreen route.
- User selects a variant → enters preview mode within the same `/user/<user-id>` workspace.
- Mobile: stacked chat + preview with toggle.

**Approve:**
- Set `websites.active_version_id`, `status=live`.
- `publishToLp` publishes to `/lp/$websiteId` (public, no auth). Inline preview config becomes live.

**Edit flow:**
1. User clicks Edit → **agent widget** opens (in chat stream) with 6 categories (multi-select):
   - Content, Logos, Media, Reviews, Contact information, Service form fields
2. Selected categories **unlock on the inline preview**: matching elements show **pencil icon**; click opens **inline editor** (contenteditable for text; upload UI for logos/media).
3. Per category behaviors:

| Category | User capability |
|---|---|
| Content | Pencil → inline text edit OR “ask AI” suggestion via same agent |
| Logos | Pencil → upload replacement / remove |
| Media | Pencil → upload **png, jpg, jpeg, webp, hevc, mp4, gif**; gallery uses same formats; mobile playback for mp4/gif |
| Reviews | Add text quote OR keep scraped (with BUSINESS-CASE attribution) |
| Contact | Edit / hide / custom contact block |
| Service form | Customize lead form fields from defaults |

4. After edits → user **returns to inline preview mode** to review before approve.
5. User **can go back** and change which edit categories are unlocked (re-open agent widget).
6. Each edit creates `website_edit_events` audit row.

**Edge cases:**
- Edit after approve → new draft version; re-approve to update live `/lp`.
- Media formats outside allowed set → reject with message.
- User changes edit categories mid-session → previously unlocked sections lock/unlock accordingly.

### 7. `/login` and `/user/<user-id>`

- **`/user/<user-id>`** — `user-id` = `profiles.id` (not `auth.users.id`).
- **`/login`:** contractor enters license **or** email → OTP → `/user/<profiles.id>`.
