## Architecture

### Route map (new)

| Route | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `/` | Marketing LP + enquiry flow (unchanged) |
| `/login` | License or email → OTP auth |
| `/user/$userId` | Agent chat + inline preview workspace |
| `/lp/$websiteId` | Public live site |
| `/admin` | Admin login + dashboard |
| `/admin/*` | Admin sub-screens |

*Deferred routes:* `/checkout`, `/onboarding/account`, `/preview/$versionId` (preview is inline in `/user/$userId`).

### Server functions (extend pattern in [`src/lib/plan-inquiry.functions.ts`](src/lib/plan-inquiry.functions.ts))

| Function | Auth | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `sendOtp` / `verifyOtp` | public | Lovable email-OTP login (license or email) for returning contractors |
| `completePostCheckout` | payment webhook / stub / admin simulate | Post-payment: persist checkout context, create pending subscription, **send OTP** — does not create auth user |
| `verifyOtpAndLinkProfile` | public (post-checkout OTP page) | Verify OTP → create auth user → link profile by license → activate subscription → redirect `/user/<profiles.id>` |
| `simulatePostCheckout` | admin / dev | v1 test path: skip payment UI, run `completePostCheckout` with license + email + name + city |
| `adminKickoff` | admin | Create license-keyed profile + website stub → `/user/<profiles.id>` |
| `adminImpersonateUser` | admin | Set impersonation cookie scoped to `profiles.id` for kickoff workspace access |
| `sendAgentMessage` | user/admin | Stream GPT-5.5 agent tokens via SSE; load journal + prompts |
| `firecrawl_scrape` | user/admin | Enqueue enrichment job chain (does not call Firecrawl inline) |
| `getJobProgress` | user/admin | Poll job chain progress % (Realtime reconnect fallback) |
| `generateSiteVariants` | user/admin | Enqueue `site_generation` job chain → 2 distinct `website_versions` |
| `publishToLp` | user/admin | Publish approved version to live `/lp/$websiteId` |
| `approveWebsiteVersion` | user | Set live + publish via `publishToLp` |
| `applyWebsiteEdits` | user | Patch config + audit |
| `submitLead` | public | Lead form on `/lp` → `leads` table |
| `adminLogin` | admin session | Operator auth |

### Agent system prompts & tool registry

**Design principle:** Agent reasoning is LLM-driven; all side effects go through **deterministic, typed tools** registered in a central tool registry. System prompts define role, guardrails, and when to call each tool — never embed scrape/publish logic in prompt text alone.

**System prompt layers:**
1. **Base agent prompt** — Obra onboarding assistant; tone; step order; required fields before generation.
2. **Persona-first design prompt** — recursively understand contractor persona from enrichment + onboarding; design site that strictly caters to that persona from first principles.
3. **Look-and-feel profile prompt** — Professional / Funky / Modern design constraints (injected per user choice).
4. **Grounding prompt** — “Only use data from `enrichment_json`, `onboarding_state`, and user messages. Never invent reviews, licenses, ratings, or business facts. Never produce two similar website variants.”
5. **Tool-use prompt** — Enumerates available tools, input schemas, and call ordering (onboarding → scrape → generate → inline preview → publish).

**First-class agent artifacts (loaded every turn):**
- System prompt (layers above)
- Tool registry (Zod schemas)
- `journal-<license-number>.md` (rolling summary; updated every 10 messages)

**Model:** GPT-5.5 via Lovable AI (configured by Lovable, same as `FIRECRAWL_API_KEY`).

**Deterministic tool registry:**

| Tool | Type | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `saveOnboardingField` | write | Persist structured onboarding field to `onboarding_state` |
| `firecrawl_scrape` | external | Firecrawl API operator — custom extraction instructions from user details; returns parsed 113-col schema |
| `getEnrichmentSummary` | read | Return grounded summary from `enrichment_json` only |
| `searchComponentLibrary` | read | Query `ui-components/manifest.json` by section type, mood, trade (returns block `id`, `storage_key`, mood/trade tags) |
| `composeSiteConfig` | write | Assemble `site_config` JSON from enrichment + component picks + theme + primary color |
| `generateVariants` | write | Produce 2 distinct `website_versions`; unselected → `discarded` in history |
| `publishToLp` | write | Publish approved version to live `/lp/$websiteId` |
| `suggestCopy` | read | AI copy suggestion for a section — output must cite source field from enrichment |
| `applyConfigPatch` | write | Apply user edit-category patches; audit to `website_edit_events` |

**Tool contract rules:**
- Every tool has a Zod input/output schema; agent cannot call tools with free-form payloads.
- `firecrawl_scrape` and `publishToLp` are server-only; API keys never exposed to client.
- Tool results are persisted before agent references them in user-facing messages.
- Failed tool calls surface explicit errors to user — agent must not mask failures with fabricated success.

### UI Component Library

**Source:** Marketing Blocks library (~2,537 HTML blocks) in **Lovable Cloud storage** (private bucket `ui-components`, prefix `marketing-blocks/`). Full block HTML is not stored in git.

**Index in repo:** [`ui-components/manifest.json`](ui-components/manifest.json) — categories, block filenames, archive paths. Bundled at build time for `searchComponentLibrary` on Cloudflare.

**Integration:** Server-only catalog ([`src/lib/agent/catalog.server.ts`](src/lib/agent/catalog.server.ts)) queries manifest by section category, mood tags (inferred from filename), and trade (category priority map). Agent queries via `searchComponentLibrary` — never loads full library into context.

**Render integration (Bucket 4+):** `site-renderer` fetches block HTML from storage by `storage_key`; maps `id` (`category/block_filename`) to rendered section.

### Agent tool-use design (summary)

Agent receives the deterministic tool registry above (not free-form HTML generation or direct HTTP calls). This keeps rendering predictable, enrichment grounded, and deploys auditable — aligns with BUSINESS-CASE “config injection” factory model.

